Caelza: Cael in the top bar, "explain this screen" on every page (vision §3.4).

The vision's first-UI list has a one-tap "explain this screen" anywhere in
the app, answered by the Guide. The button is Cael's look in the top bar
(overlay web/src/guide/CaelButton.tsx); the panel says what the screen is
and the next step in his words with no model needed, and below that the
owner can ask him anything about it: the answer streams from the `cael`
agent over the gateway's chat socket in one guide conversation the browser
keeps. These hunks put the button in the top bar beside the settings gear,
add the strings (English; the other locales fall back: one paragraph and
one next step per screen, and the panel's own) and list the logic test
beside the others. Applied after 0011 and the overlay copy.

